# OnCongaTimeout Property

Applies to:{.prefix}

Server{.info}

The OnCongaTimeout property specifies a call back function to be called whenever the server
performs housekeeping: when the Conga wait times out, and on a busy server when an event arrives
once →[CongaTimeout] milliseconds have passed since housekeeping last ran. This function is
expected to exist in the namespace or object instance defined by the →[Context] property. This
callback may be the name of a method of some class.

The callback runs in the server thread, before the event that prompted it is handled, so it should
be brief. Anything lengthy belongs in a thread of the application's own.

The right argument provided to the function is a →[##.##.Server] object. 

The result of the callback should be 0.

